silm:instances_papers_11_base_commutative_diagram_chapters_26_circuit_imprint_tensor_sections_02_eight_corners_atlas_concrete_anchor_4#corner_100 silm:hasLongDescription "The Corner_100 is [physical, class, classification]: taxonomist working with physical specimens at class level -- TSN 183798 as a class taxonomic node. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'Corner_100', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
